  "rationale": "The only directly applicable measured optimization is Maven dependency caching (P-LIT-CONFIG-REUSE / P-LIT-GHA-CACHE), which the experiment demonstrated by adding actions/cache@v4 for ~/.m2/repository (~51% elapsed savings). The target workflow already provides the equivalent cache via actions/setup-java@v4 with cache: 'maven', which caches the same ~/.m2/repository. Adding a second explicit actions/cache entry for the same path would be redundant, risk cache thrashing, and would not preserve or improve build/test coverage. The matrix contains a single Java version (21) with fail-fast: false, so matrix-cancellation optimizations (P-LIT-FAIL-FAST) are not applicable. No other measured, safe optimization applies without weakening required checks or introducing unrelated changes.",
  "evidence_ids": ["experiment:batch-hiruni-pattern-bat-a89d5fd8d30bc8cb-r2", "pattern:P-LIT-GHA-CACHE", "pattern:P-LIT-CONFIG-REUSE"]
}
